ounty&rsquo;s 6 grids in Lincoln County came in under 90% of normal in October to November in 38 of 75 years since 1951, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, the middle ran 45% of normal in January to February and 56% in March to April. Grid 16954 shows a preliminary estimate of 48.4 for August to September 2026, an estimate from NOAA rain that RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ from. Grid 16953 had its driest year in 2010 at 61% of normal.</p>"}
